1
00:00:03,970 --> 00:00:07,440
Oh, damn, they canceled my Visa.

2
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:11,210
Oh, yay, a new MasterCard!

3
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:14,510
What?

4
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:16,410
I was going to get my mail.

5
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:18,210
Okay.

6
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:23,350
Are... are you hoping to get it telepathically?

7
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:26,210
I think you mean telekinetically.

8
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:28,050
And no.

9
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:30,230
I just wasn't sure of the proper protocol

10
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:32,740
now that you and Leonard are no longer having coitus.

11
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:36,590
God, can we please just say "no longer seeing each other"?

12
00:00:36,590 --> 00:00:38,100
Well, we could if it were true.

13
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,540
But as you live in the same building, you see each other all the time.

14
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:44,870
The variable which has changed is the coitus.

15
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:50,230
Okay, here's the protocol: you and I are still friends, and you stop saying "coitus."

16
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:51,960
Good, good.

17
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:53,920
I'm glad we're still friends.

18
00:00:53,930 --> 00:00:54,870
Really?

19
00:00:54,870 --> 00:00:58,220
Oh, yes. It was a lot of work to accommodate you in my life.

20
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:01,570
I'd hate for that effort to have been in vain.

21
00:01:01,570 --> 00:01:02,920
Right.

22
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:07,840
Just to be clear, do I have to stop saying "coitus" with everyone or just you?

23
00:01:08,290 --> 00:01:10,450
Everyone.

24
00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:11,970
Harsh terms.

25
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:14,390
But all right-- I'll just substitute "intercourse."

26
00:01:14,390 --> 00:01:15,580
Great.

27
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:16,950
Or "fornication."

28
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:21,230
Yeah. But that has judgmental overtones, so I'll hold that in reserve.

29
00:01:21,230 --> 00:01:23,420
So, how you been?

30
00:01:23,420 --> 00:01:26,400
Well, my existence is a continuum,

31
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:30,770
so I've been what I am at each point in the implied time period.

32
00:01:32,410 --> 00:01:35,430
You're just coitusing with me, aren't you?

33
00:01:37,690 --> 00:01:39,940
Bazinga.

34
00:01:41,850 --> 00:01:43,090
How's Leonard doing?

35
00:01:43,090 --> 00:01:44,540
He seems all right.

36
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:47,220
Although he does spend a disturbing amount of time

37
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:48,910
looking at photographs of you

38
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:52,300
and smelling the pillow you slept on.

39
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:53,780
Oh, but now that I think of it,

40
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:56,900
he asked me not to tell you that.

41
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:59,180
I'll pretend I didn't hear it.

42
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:03,140
I'd rather you pretend I didn't say it.

43
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:07,030
I see you bought Mama Italia marinara spaghetti sauce.

44
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:08,610
Yep.

45
00:02:08,610 --> 00:02:10,830
That's the sauce my mother uses.

46
00:02:10,830 --> 00:02:13,140
She likes cooking Italian because according to her,

47
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:16,830
that's what the Romans made Jesus eat.

48
00:02:16,830 --> 00:02:18,170
Interesting.

49
00:02:18,170 --> 00:02:20,780
I'll have to have you over for spaghetti some night.

50
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:22,290
I'm hungry now.

51
00:02:22,890 --> 00:02:24,970
Oh. Um, okay.

52
00:02:24,970 --> 00:02:27,040
Why don't you give me an hour and come over?

53
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:31,510
Will you cut up hot dogs into little chunks and mix them in with the sauce?

54
00:02:31,510 --> 00:02:33,080
I don't have hot dogs.

55
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:34,320
Oh, it's all right; I do.

56
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:38,680
Oh! You're in for what my mother calls "a real Eye-talian treat".

57
00:02:42,330 --> 00:02:43,400
Hey, where you been?

58
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:45,540
I was talking with Penny.

59
00:02:45,550 --> 00:02:47,350
What's wrong with you?

60
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:49,460
You can't hang out with your roommate's ex.

61
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:50,970
That's totally uncool.

62
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:53,050
No, it's fine. I don't care.

63
00:02:53,050 --> 00:02:54,760
I'm over it.

64
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:57,240
Yeah, he's over it; that's why he's been whining all day

65
00:02:57,240 --> 00:03:00,790
about trying to invent that memory-wiper gizmo from Men in Black.

66
00:03:00,790 --> 00:03:02,760
Is he making any progress?

67
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:06,410
Because I'd like to erase Ben Affleck as Daredevil.

68
00:03:09,330 --> 00:03:11,500
So would Ben Affleck.

69
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:15,790
The point is, in a situation like this you got to pick sides.

70
00:03:15,790 --> 00:03:18,270
You're either on Team Leonard or Team Penny.

71
00:03:18,270 --> 00:03:20,710
Which one picks last?

72
00:03:20,710 --> 00:03:22,250
What?

73
00:03:22,250 --> 00:03:24,730
Well, usually I'm on the team that picks last.

74
00:03:25,770 --> 00:03:28,510
Unless there's a kid in a wheelchair.

75
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:32,990
Sheldon, I got you your tangerine chicken.

76
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,440
I hope you're hungry.

77
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:37,480
Well, of course I'm hungry.

78
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:40,760
And as I have no plans to eat with any other team,

79
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:44,640
I will consume my tangerine chicken with the appropriate gusto.

80
00:03:48,590 --> 00:03:49,860
Okay.

81
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:52,680
Just out of curiosity, do we still have hot dogs?

82
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:54,580
I don't know. Why?

83
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:56,990
Just making dinner conversation.

84
00:03:56,990 --> 00:03:59,870
Go, Team Leonard!

85
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:26,870
Oh, God, this is good.

86
00:04:26,870 --> 00:04:28,540
Let me ask you a question.

87
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:30,440
Do you believe you're going to go to hell

88
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:32,670
for eating sweet and sour pork?

89
00:04:32,670 --> 00:04:35,210
Jews don't have hell.

90
00:04:35,210 --> 00:04:38,480
We have acid reflux.

91
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:41,280
Do you want the last dumpling, Sheldon?

92
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,580
Certainly.

93
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:44,610
It's not like I have to moderate my food intake

94
00:04:44,610 --> 00:04:47,210
because I'm planning on eating again very shortly.

95
00:04:53,590 --> 00:04:55,340
So, you guys want to do something tonight?

96
00:04:55,430 --> 00:04:58,940
Nah, I can't. I got to pick up my mom from her water aerobics class.

97
00:04:59,030 --> 00:05:05,900
18 overweight women flapping their arm fat in a swimming pool.

98
00:05:07,110 --> 00:05:11,170
Looks like the manatee tank at Sea World.

99
00:05:12,410 --> 00:05:13,940
What about you, Raj?

100
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:15,280
Oh, there it is:

101
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:16,710
now that you don't have a girlfriend,

102
00:05:16,710 --> 00:05:18,680
you want to hang out with me again.

103
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:21,180
- I never stopped hanging out with you. - Oh, please,

104
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:24,350
we all know I'm the friend you call when you have no other options.

105
00:05:24,350 --> 00:05:28,020
If we were the Justice League, I'd be Aquaman.

106
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:29,970
I wish you were Aquaman.

107
00:05:29,970 --> 00:05:33,670
Then I could send you to scoop my mom out of the old lady tank.

108
00:05:35,310 --> 00:05:39,280
Excuse me, I'm thirsty, so I'm going to go to the refrigerator

109
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:42,110
and get myself a refreshing beverage.

110
00:05:43,380 --> 00:05:46,880
You know what? I'll just spend the evening alone.

111
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:50,890
What, suddenly I'm not good enough for you?

112
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:01,190
I do so love beverages.

113
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:05,130
Now I think I'll take my after-dinner walk.

114
00:06:08,330 --> 00:06:10,900
Since when do you take after-dinner walks?

115
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:13,000
Yeah, since when do you take walks?

116
00:06:13,010 --> 00:06:15,810
I read a study online that walking after a meal

117
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:18,610
not only aids in digestion, but increases serotonin,

118
00:06:18,610 --> 00:06:21,340
and you know me, if there's one thing I like

119
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:24,110
more than a refreshing beverage, it's serotonin. Bye-bye.

120
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:26,420
Hold on. I'll walk down with you.

121
00:06:27,490 --> 00:06:29,320
That's not necessary.

122
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:31,650
You can go first.

123
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,060
Or we could go together.

124
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:36,960
I can't think of a reason why not.

125
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:38,060
Let's go.

126
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:39,530
Hold on.

127
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:41,700
Nope, no reason.

128
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:52,610
I've missed you.

129
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:57,850
All right, say hello to your mother for me.

130
00:06:57,850 --> 00:07:00,110
Okay.

131
00:07:03,790 --> 00:07:05,720
What?

132
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:08,490
You said you were going for a walk.

133
00:07:08,490 --> 00:07:11,190
I didn't say outside.

134
00:07:11,190 --> 00:07:15,330
So what, you're just gonna walk up and down the stairs?

135
00:07:15,330 --> 00:07:17,900
No, of course not.

136
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:20,770
That would be odd and suspicious behavior.

137
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:23,770
Here, Russell! Here, boy!

138
00:07:23,770 --> 00:07:25,230
Which way are you going?

139
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:26,740
Which way are "you" going?

140
00:07:26,740 --> 00:07:29,200
I parked my scooter down the block.

141
00:07:29,210 --> 00:07:32,170
I'm going the other way. Bye.

142
00:07:32,170 --> 00:07:33,670
Bye.

143
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:36,710
Actually, I'm this way.

144
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:39,850
Do I smell hot dogs?

145
00:07:39,850 --> 00:07:42,780
No. I mean, I have no idea what you smell.

146
00:07:43,580 --> 00:07:45,820
I definitely smell raw hot dog.

147
00:07:46,650 --> 00:07:48,120
Perhaps you're getting a brain tumor.

148
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:51,420
All right, have a nice walk.

149
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:53,790
I shall. Have a nice scoot.

150
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:57,760
You might want to stand back.

151
00:07:57,760 --> 00:08:01,160
I'm sitting on top of 13 horses here.

152
00:08:11,770 --> 00:08:13,500
Oh. Hello, doggie.

153
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:15,170
Nice doggie.

154
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:19,970
I bet you think you smell hot dogs.

155
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,640
Look, a cat!

156
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:29,770
Penny?

157
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,770
Penny.

158
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:39,240
Penny.

159
00:08:40,110 --> 00:08:41,580
Here.

160
00:08:43,350 --> 00:08:46,610
I had to trade the others for my life.

161
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,540
Hey, Leonard?

162
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:54,840
Yeah?

163
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:57,210
I haven't had sex in a year.

164
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:02,510
Where you going with this, Raj?

165
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:05,480
Don't flatter yourself, dude.

166
00:09:07,150 --> 00:09:08,780
I want to go out and meet a woman.

167
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:10,480
- So, go.  - Well, I need a wingman.

168
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:13,850
I don't want to come off like a lonely loser.

169
00:09:13,850 --> 00:09:17,360
And you think "my" presence will help with that?

170
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:18,660
Well, I do.

171
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:21,360
Next to you, I'll look like a catch.

172
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:23,930
I'm not going out tonight, Raj.

173
00:09:23,930 --> 00:09:25,530
All right.

174
00:09:25,530 --> 00:09:27,060
Would you mind if I went to your room

175
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:30,170
and downloaded some Asian pornography?

176
00:09:30,170 --> 00:09:32,700
Very much.

177
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:34,700
Doesn't have to be Asian.

178
00:09:36,670 --> 00:09:38,540
Don't worry. You'll meet a girl someday.

179
00:09:38,540 --> 00:09:41,680
- No, I won't.  - Yes, you will, and she'll be beautiful.

180
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:43,680
And kind and sexy and funny

181
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:45,510
and everything you ever wanted in a woman.

182
00:09:45,510 --> 00:09:46,580
You really think so?

183
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:50,320
I do, and you'll fall hopelessly in love and give her your heart.

184
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:54,190
And she'll take it and grind it into pathetic, little pieces.

185
00:09:55,590 --> 00:09:57,590
But we'll have sex first, right?

186
00:10:11,140 --> 00:10:13,670
That's Eye-talian.

187
00:10:13,670 --> 00:10:17,370
So, um, was Leonard okay with you coming over?

188
00:10:17,370 --> 00:10:19,240
Oh, yes.

189
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:22,040
In fact, he said, "I'm fine. I don't care."

190
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:23,880
And he in no way said it in a manner

191
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:25,750
which would lead one to believe that he was covering up

192
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:27,680
feelings of anguish and betrayal.

193
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:30,690
- Well, good.  - I'm also

194
00:10:30,690 --> 00:10:34,420
pleased to report that he's all cried out over you.

195
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:35,960
He's been crying?

196
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:38,190
Oh, I believe that was something else

197
00:10:38,190 --> 00:10:39,560
I wasn't supposed to mention.

198
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:42,860
Oh, God, I feel terrible.

199
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:45,130
Do you have a stomachache, too?

200
00:10:45,130 --> 00:10:46,770
No. Why, do you?

201
00:10:46,770 --> 00:10:49,470
No.

202
00:10:49,470 --> 00:10:52,170
Why did you ask if I had one, too?

203
00:10:52,170 --> 00:10:55,210
Just making polite dinner conversation.

204
00:10:55,210 --> 00:10:56,570
Your turn.

205
00:10:56,570 --> 00:10:59,810
All right.

206
00:10:59,810 --> 00:11:01,980
So, what's new in your life?

207
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:07,420
Well, my new shoes are not made for running.

208
00:11:09,250 --> 00:11:11,250
Have you been running?

209
00:11:11,250 --> 00:11:13,990
No.

210
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:17,060
It's just a suspicion I have.

211
00:11:21,930 --> 00:11:24,730
- I'm so glad you like it.  -I do.

212
00:11:24,730 --> 00:11:26,530
Leonard never cooks for me.

213
00:11:26,530 --> 00:11:28,930
Well, maybe that's 'cause Leonard can't cook.

214
00:11:28,930 --> 00:11:31,470
You can't cook and you made me this.

215
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,370
Whatever.

216
00:11:34,370 --> 00:11:36,410
Ooh, I'm gonna get the cheesecake out of the fridge.

217
00:11:37,540 --> 00:11:39,910
Oh, Lord, I'm in Jewish hell.

218
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:48,600
Look at this.

219
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:50,200
Do you think she's really doing that

220
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:52,370
or is it PhotoShop?

221
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:57,940
I'm pretty sure Martha Stewart never got naked

222
00:11:57,940 --> 00:12:01,010
with a room full of big, fat Japanese guys.

223
00:12:01,010 --> 00:12:03,540
You don't know that.

224
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:06,580
Prison changes people.

225
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:10,100
Hey, where you been?

226
00:12:10,110 --> 00:12:13,310
I told you, walking.

227
00:12:13,310 --> 00:12:14,470
For an hour and a half?

228
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:16,840
I got lost.

229
00:12:17,980 --> 00:12:20,310
How could you get lost? Your phone has GPS.

230
00:12:20,310 --> 00:12:24,150
Satellites are down. Solar flares.

231
00:12:24,150 --> 00:12:25,550
There are no solar flares right now.

232
00:12:25,550 --> 00:12:26,780
Yes, there are.

233
00:12:26,790 --> 00:12:28,150
Dude, I'm an astrophysicist.

234
00:12:28,150 --> 00:12:30,650
If there were solar flares, I'd be all up in it.

235
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:34,690
I'm sorry. I misspoke.

236
00:12:34,690 --> 00:12:37,560
What I meant to say was my battery died.

237
00:12:40,130 --> 00:12:41,730
What the hell was that about?

238
00:12:41,730 --> 00:12:43,200
I don't know.

239
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:46,570
Do you think this is really Hillary Clinton doing it with Oprah?

240
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:51,100
Oh, we really need to get you a girl.

241
00:12:55,210 --> 00:12:56,540
Leonard.

242
00:12:57,710 --> 00:12:58,910
Leonard.

243
00:12:58,910 --> 00:13:00,180
Leonard.

244
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:01,610
Oh, just come in!

245
00:13:03,050 --> 00:13:06,790
Thanks for seeing me on such short notice.

246
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:11,360
What do you want, Sheldon?

247
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:14,030
Maybe this isn't a good time.

248
00:13:14,030 --> 00:13:17,860
Tell me why you woke me up or I swear to God I will kill you.

249
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:20,530
Do you really think death threats

250
00:13:20,530 --> 00:13:22,700
are an appropriate way to begin this conversation?

251
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:26,800
Sometimes your lack of social skills astonishes me.

252
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:30,870
What do you want?

253
00:13:30,870 --> 00:13:34,070
You may want to sit down.

254
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:35,880
I'm in bed!

255
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:38,040
Point taken.

256
00:13:38,050 --> 00:13:39,350
You may want to sit up.

257
00:13:39,350 --> 00:13:42,080
Sheldon!

258
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:45,720
I've been seeing Penny behind your back.

259
00:13:53,220 --> 00:13:56,160
Okay...

260
00:13:56,160 --> 00:14:01,060
When you say "seeing Penny," what exactly does that mean?

261
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:03,330
We had dinner last night.

262
00:14:03,330 --> 00:14:06,300
She made me spaghetti with little hot dogs cut up in it.

263
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:08,170
Well, little hot dog.

264
00:14:08,170 --> 00:14:11,170
I gave up the other five hot dogs to a real dog.

265
00:14:11,170 --> 00:14:12,510
A real, big dog.

266
00:14:13,410 --> 00:14:15,440
A hell hound.

267
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:17,140
Tangential to the primary story.

268
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:19,240
How about I circle back to it?

269
00:14:19,250 --> 00:14:21,380
Fine.

270
00:14:21,380 --> 00:14:23,280
Why did you have dinner with Penny?

271
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:25,380
I told you, she made spaghetti with little hot dogs.

272
00:14:25,390 --> 00:14:27,750
I like spaghetti with little hot dogs.

273
00:14:27,750 --> 00:14:30,950
Then why did you have Chinese food with us?

274
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:32,790
I didn't want to upset you.

275
00:14:32,790 --> 00:14:35,520
Howard made it very clear that my allegiance should be

276
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:39,690
to male comrades before women who sell their bodies for money.

277
00:14:41,730 --> 00:14:45,800
Is it possible he said, "Bros before hos"?

278
00:14:46,870 --> 00:14:50,440
Yes, but I rephrased it to avoid offending the hos.

279
00:14:52,210 --> 00:14:55,780
Sheldon, I don't care if you want to be friends with Penny.

280
00:14:55,780 --> 00:15:00,410
Oh. Well, so the emotional turmoil that's been keeping me

281
00:15:00,410 --> 00:15:03,450
from achieving REM sleep was entirely unjustified?

282
00:15:03,450 --> 00:15:05,450
Yes.

283
00:15:05,450 --> 00:15:09,020
Well... then as my meemaw would say,

284
00:15:09,020 --> 00:15:12,320
"Looks like we butchered a pig, but nobody wanted bacon."

285
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:16,260
I guess not.

286
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:19,160
And now, as promised, the tangent.

287
00:15:20,570 --> 00:15:22,600
Sheldon and the Hell Hound.

288
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:25,460
Or How I Lost My Hot Dogs.

289
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:32,570
I, I can come back.

290
00:15:32,570 --> 00:15:34,070
D-don't be silly.

291
00:15:34,070 --> 00:15:35,170
We're neighbors.

292
00:15:35,170 --> 00:15:36,370
We're going to run into each other.

293
00:15:36,370 --> 00:15:37,540
May as well get used to it.

294
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:40,540
Yeah, I guess you're right.

295
00:15:46,550 --> 00:15:47,750
You used to it yet?

296
00:15:47,750 --> 00:15:49,650
- Nope. - Me neither.

297
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:54,050
Oh, Sheldon seemed to think that I would be upset

298
00:15:54,050 --> 00:15:55,190
about you hanging out with him.

299
00:15:55,190 --> 00:15:56,720
But I just want you to know it's fine.

300
00:15:56,720 --> 00:15:59,920
Oh, oh, good, because, um, his mother called me.

301
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,390
His mother?

302
00:16:02,390 --> 00:16:05,930
Yeah, she wants me to take him shopping for sheets and towels.

303
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:08,630
I was going to do that.

304
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:11,830
Oh, well, then you... you do it.

305
00:16:11,830 --> 00:16:13,940
No, I don't want to do it. You can do it.

306
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:16,240
Okay, you can take him for shoes.

307
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:18,310
I just took him for shoes.

308
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:21,410
Well, all I know is he says they hurt his feet.

309
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:27,150
Fine. I'll take him for shoes next Saturday.

310
00:16:27,150 --> 00:16:29,210
Oh, no, no, no-- a bunch of us from work

311
00:16:29,210 --> 00:16:30,620
are going to Disneyland next Saturday

312
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:31,980
and Sheldon wants to come.

313
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:34,720
You're taking him to Disneyland?

314
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:36,790
Well, he heard me making plans on the phone.

315
00:16:36,790 --> 00:16:39,320
Was I going to say "no"?

316
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:41,620
All right.

317
00:16:41,630 --> 00:16:43,690
But let me know if you're going to stuff him with junk food.

318
00:16:43,690 --> 00:16:47,760
I don't want to bring home a nice dinner for him and see it go to waste.

319
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:50,600
We're going to Disneyland.

320
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:52,370
He's going to eat junk food.

321
00:16:52,370 --> 00:16:55,670
All I'm saying is give me a heads-up.

322
00:16:55,670 --> 00:16:57,370
Okay, whatever.

323
00:16:58,910 --> 00:17:01,540
And don't let him go on Space Mountain after he eats.

324
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:03,340
He'll say he can handle it, but I promise

325
00:17:03,340 --> 00:17:05,310
you'll end up with churro puke on your shoes.

326
00:17:05,310 --> 00:17:08,210
All right, got it. Is there anything else?

327
00:17:08,210 --> 00:17:09,610
Yeah, don't let Goofy near him.

328
00:17:09,610 --> 00:17:12,450
He'll have nightmares and I'll have to deal with it.

329
00:17:12,450 --> 00:17:14,050
What's the problem with Goofy?

330
00:17:14,050 --> 00:17:17,220
Wish I knew. He's fine with Pluto.

331
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:24,500
Hey, do you think the elastic woman in The Incredibles

332
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:28,570
needs to use birth control or can she just be a diaphragm?

333
00:17:31,540 --> 00:17:32,710
Well, that's it.

334
00:17:32,710 --> 00:17:34,710
We're officially out of things to talk about.

335
00:17:35,650 --> 00:17:37,810
We're home.

336
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:41,670
It's 10:00.Where have you been?

337
00:17:41,670 --> 00:17:44,490
We stayed for the California Adventure water show.

338
00:17:44,490 --> 00:17:46,860
It was pure Disney magic.

339
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:49,320
I was going to see that with him.

340
00:17:49,330 --> 00:17:50,930
How was I supposed to know that?

341
00:17:50,930 --> 00:17:53,260
It's all right. I'll see it again with you.

342
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:55,460
And I have food here. You said you were going to call.

343
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:56,760
I know, I know.

344
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:57,730
I can still eat.

345
00:17:57,730 --> 00:17:58,900
No, you already threw up once.

346
00:17:58,900 --> 00:18:00,800
Go put on your PJs and brush your teeth.

347
00:18:03,300 --> 00:18:05,170
Okay, but just don't fight

348
00:18:05,170 --> 00:18:07,310
- We're not fighting. - Just go.

349
00:18:10,210 --> 00:18:12,540
Aren't you going to thank Penny for taking you to Disneyland?

350
00:18:12,540 --> 00:18:14,910
Thank you, Penny.

351
00:18:15,850 --> 00:18:18,180
You're welcome, sweetie.

352
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,980
Want a cup of coffee?

353
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:23,320
Oh, um, I should probably get going.

354
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:27,660
Come on. It's just a cup of coffee.

355
00:18:34,130 --> 00:18:38,260
Uh, yeah, the whole thing seems a little twisted to me, too.

356
00:18:38,270 --> 00:18:40,400
What am I smelling?

357
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:42,830
Sheldon's churro on my shoes.

358
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:00,980
He's such an angel when he's asleep.

359
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:02,850
Yeah.

360
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:05,020
Shame he has to wake up.

361
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:09,590
I think we can do it.

362
00:19:09,590 --> 00:19:14,130
Smother Sheldon in his sleep?Wouldn't that be wrong?

363
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:18,300
No, be friends. You and me.

364
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:21,230
Oh. Sure.

365
00:19:21,230 --> 00:19:22,870
Absolutely.

366
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:25,240
Good. I'm glad.

367
00:19:26,670 --> 00:19:28,610
Here's an idea. I'm just throwing it out there:

368
00:19:28,610 --> 00:19:30,770
friends who have sex.

369
00:19:32,810 --> 00:19:35,140
Good night, Leonard.

370
00:19:35,150 --> 00:19:36,780
Kidding.

371
00:19:36,780 --> 00:19:39,150
Just a couple of friends Goofing around.

372
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:41,880
No, Goofy, no.

